Ladybird’s windows API derives windows from the tabs an extension
can see, so a private window doesn’t exist for an extension not
allowed there, and a background page’s current window is the one
last focused — as Chromium’s WindowsGetCurrentFunction answers for
a page with no window of its own. get(WINDOW_ID_CURRENT) answers
the same, and the errors (“No window with id: N.”, “No current
window”, “No last-focused window”) keep Chromium’s wording from its
ExtensionTabUtil and tabs_constants.h.
